#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:5
#: 8e4ce963b7d2485295a4653787535b50
msgid "CubePilot Here+ RTK GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:7
#: 499cd71ea3df4ab9b8fc5be4f21b5fff
msgid "This article provides a brief overview of how to setup a Here+ RTK GPS receiver which is based on the Ublox M8P. Like other RTK GPSs, the Here+ can provide much more accurate position estimates than regular GPSs but normally requires the use of a 2nd GPS connected to the ground station. These instructions focus on the setup using Mission Planner on Windows, but HERE+ is also supported by QGroundControl."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:15
#: 4cb3e92e4f7d4edf8f80063accbef940
msgid "Where to buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:17
#: d737909e9c8c4efca355e2196eeed598
msgid "Newer generation of this product can be purchased through CubePilot `resellers <https://cubepilot.org/#/reseller/list>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:20
#: 1f1b7ca4996d4bc1af1dcf1d721b9214
msgid "Connecting the vehicle and base station GPSs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:22
#: 25b1c528c60f4819bb7cd0f1bd26df0e
msgid "The Here+ GPS kit comes with a larger round GPS (also knows as the \"Rover\") that should be mounted on the vehicle so that the round button is on the top and the faint arrow is pointing forwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:24
#: 5de48a9a06a44a6ba1a5fe521af21c5a
msgid "This GPS is connected to the autopilot using the supplied 8-pin clickmate connector (if using a Cube) or an optional 4pin+6pin DF13 connector (if using Pixhawk)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:26
#: a77ac650b517450da2078d14878d8190
msgid "A smaller GPS (also known as the \"base station\") labelled \"here+\" is also included along with its external antenna.  This GPS is connected to the ground station PC using the supplied USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:28
#: 6f430f51be6f42058583081aa92cca33
msgid "Below is a diagram showing how to connect the Here+ to a Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:34
#: 89fbdc1cb74449fe923489e5e5f31976
msgid "Installing the Drivers and U-Center"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:36
#: a82ae4b7082c4186ab63542ee3959d38
msgid "Windows  users  will need to download and install the `u-blox u-center application and drivers <https://www.u-blox.com/en/product/u-center>`__ in order to update the firmware to The new version of 1.30 firmware which includes new feature of fusing other satellite systems (Glonass / beidou) with GPS for RTK operations, effectively increasing the RTK positioning accuracy. Therefore, it is recommended that all users upgrade to 1.30 or later firmware before using HERE+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:38
#: bea9a747321841129fe23e5840a77eca
msgid "If installed correctly, when plugged in, the GPS should appear in the Device Manager as \"USB Serial Device\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:44
#: fd9fb3cd8f4b4145ba8e7b57edbbd648
msgid "Upgrading U-blox Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:45
#: de99f6fea6c845f19c3ef08686bd2fc5
msgid "The default firmware version of the HERE + modules is ublox-1.10 firmware. The newer version of 1.30  or later firmware includes new feature of fusing other satellite systems (Glonass / beidou) with GPS for RTK operations, effectively increasing the RTK positioning accuracy. Therefore, it is recommended that all users upgrade to 1.30 or later firmware before using HERE+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:47
#: e784178390714f1ba85125a44ebe786a
msgid "Later versions have also been released. 1.40 version firmware introduced a new feature called the mobile base station, that is, the base station need not be fixed in a location. For example, a base station may be placed on a moving vehicle or boat. Upgrading to Ublox-1.40 version is similar to upgrading to 1.30. For users who do not need to use the mobile baseline feature, upgrading to version 1.30 is sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:49
#: 49f7c8662d67472aae73fdafd6899e2d
msgid "Firmware releases can be found `here <https://www.u-blox.com/en/product/neo-m8p-series?legacy=Current#Documentation-&-resources>`__. Download the base (reference) and/or rover version , as appropriate to use in the following step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:52
#: ba71b05956d84a06bfab797273fb799e
msgid "Upgrading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:53
#: 7ecd2e781a3e4a1396772b0313502fed
msgid "Upgrading firmware requires the use of Ublox's Windows software U-center. To download U-center, please go to the `official website <https://www.u-blox.com/en/product/u-center-windows>`__. Then follow the prompts to install U-cent software. During the installation process, you will be prompted to install the device Driver, please ensure that only the Standard Driver For Windows is checked, as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:60
#: 972bb48335dd41389f8e1f3bf5115ef5
msgid "Connect your HERE+ Base and Rover to Computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:61
#: 77e767bd316a433ba7ab8e8905a42232
msgid "When upgrading the base station module, use the USB cable to connect the base station module to the computer USB interface, as shown in the following figure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:66
#: ddd4397c02444b35b802ec7393f52ff4
msgid "When upgrading a Rover module, use a hexagonal screwdriver to open the case. The rover module has a USB interface connector identical to the base module, you can use the base module USB cable to connect rover to computer. In addition, during the firmware upgrading process, the rover module needs to be powered by connecting to autopilot, as shown in the following figure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:73
#: 1660ff181b7b493a81b094feec2bdc9f
msgid "Upgrading Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:74
#: 75cff3554e0343b29db5b64b3e81719d
msgid "Open the U-center software, click the connection button (as shown in the red circle), select the com port that corresponds to your base/ rover module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:79
#: 2f23b3f708ad4ddc9cfe525a3f838ac6
msgid "Click tools->u-blox 5 – 8 Flash Firmware Update, and click the settings as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:88
#: c3b1c08614e54e9e9ac88b80360c1a97
msgid "In Flash Information Structure(FIS) File, select Flash.xml，which is located in the installation address of U-centre software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:93
#: 67228705b3814fc68066823b0d517db6
msgid "Click OK and wait for the firmware uploading to complete. Uploading usually takes only a minute or less. If the uploading is successful, the upgrade interface is displayed in green; if the upgrade is aborted, the interface is displayed in red. If the process is interrupted, or if it is not responding for a long time, the modules will need to be power cycled and uploading needs to be done again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:96
#: f262dc270ae441bab54b6e147ed3d8a6
msgid "Check current Rover/Base firmware version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:97
#: 8647ad7c67da487e9e3b254254265568
msgid "When base/rover is already connected to U-center, click View, go to Message View -> UBX -> MON _> VER, you will see the interface below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:102
#: e300aaff7f1c480aa1d610287f132f0a
msgid "As shown in the figure, the current firmware version is FWVER = HPG 1.30 REF, indicating that the current firmware version is 1.30 for base module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:105
#: c8b0d1ddf82147b8a2ea95c0fb8efeb3
msgid "Basic operating manual"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:106
#: 785ee24320004c3280640cc9474190c2
msgid "This part of the tutorial uses Mission Planner ground control software and ArduCopter-3.5 flight control firmware for operating instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:109
#: 23c1986a4ba54d2b8c55c0dce964d10e
msgid "Preparation before operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:110
#: 245e2ecd3a884ec4b729c35207b57702
msgid "To use HERE+ on a UAV, you need the following hardware:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:115
#: 9bc06fcb58634f58a13dadf3464f6a24
msgid "Before using, make sure the hardware is connected correctly: The base station module is connected to the computer port through USB; a telemetry module is connected to another USB port of the same computer. For UAV, HERE + rover module is connected to the autopilot GPS connector, telemetry module is connected to the TELEM interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:120
#: 0806cd0d4d2042c8b29b9fbf46b8ce54
msgid "Place vehicle and base stations so that their GPS antennas have a clear view of the sky (i.e. this will not work indoors!)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:121
#: f9c17cdb89f44aaa95388032e137171b
msgid "During operation, please place the base station in an outdoor environment with sufficient sky coverage to obtain a good satellite signal. Place the base station on a stable and elevated platform, such as a tripod."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:126
#: 47d7d90cbd97454f9735a596f94a7cdd
msgid "Connect to the vehicle's autopilot (i.e. Pixhawk, Cube, etc) using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:127
#: 55da66320d16433d974012017be606eb
msgid "Open the Initial Setup >> Optional Hardware >> RTK GPS Inject screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:128
#: ef9994e8d16a4656b858fcdb52d56ecf
msgid "For first time setup in a new location, click the Enter Base Position button, make sure the dialog box shows empty location information, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:134
#: 8e9e704fd8c1457c8d71aece267b06c5
msgid "Base module setting using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:135
#: e672af9e22c74c29a84b8ffb1f9da209
msgid "Start with base module setup first. During the base station setup, the rover and the UAV do not need to be turned on. Open the Mission Planner ground station software on your computer and go to the initial setup -> Optional Hardware -> RTK / GPS Inject page. You will see the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:140
#: 3dd755a55f2e4778a4e8d834c35ab343
msgid "Select the correct base module com port in the top left corner and click connect. In the SurveyIn Acc section, enter the absolute geographic accuracy that you expect your HERE + base station to achieve. In the Time column, enter the minimum survey time you expect. Click on Restart, the ground station will transfer the data you have entered to the HERE + base module, the base module will start a new round of surveying. You will see the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:145
#: e6d590495f1449ce93246668420e3932
msgid "During the survey process, the right box will show the current survey status: Position is invalid: base station has not yet reached a valid location; In Progress: survey is still in progress; Duration: The number of seconds that the current surveying task has been executed; Observation: the number of observations acquired; Current Acc: Absolute geographic accuracy that the current base station can achieve. The green bar at the lower part of the Mission Planner page shows the satellites being detected and the signal strength related to each satellite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:147
#: fae3d1a7cadf4631bf8d35b86cc6c287
msgid "The base station needs a certain amount of time to meet the accuracy requirements of your input. Testing shows that, in an open area without shelter, to achieve the absolute accuracy of 2m takes a few minutes; to reach the absolute accuracy of less than 30cm takes around an hour; to reach the accuracy of 10cm takes a few hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:151
#: ab41ce6f997747279a2e1939f482c4c3
msgid "These duration could vary greatly by various factors. For example, to achieve the absolute accuracy of 2m could take an hour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:153
#: 7faea44dd48f4929a4bf1890a086f413
msgid "It should be noted that the absolute geographic accuracy of the base station here will affect the absolute geographic accuracy of the rover module without affecting the relative accuracy between the base station and rover. If your application does not require UAV with high absolute geographic accuracy, you do not need to set the base station's precision too high, resulting in long survey time. Even if the accuracy of the base station is 1.5 to 2 m, the position accuracy of the rover module relative to the base station can still reach centimeter level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:155
#: 35018214b0834e56ac7b3b7b9268db2a
msgid "After the survey is complete, Mission Planner will display the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:160
#: f6a349aef2f345c981ffe88fe37b2c9b
msgid "In the RTCM box is shows that the base status indicator is green and both the GPS and Glonass satellite systems are green (if you want to change the satellite system, refer to the following section). The box on the right says Position is valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:162
#: 34b934ec91ea4b9592d087184ff01da5
msgid "To store the current location in the Mission Planner: Click Save Current Pos, enter a name in the dialog box, and click OK. As shown below, you can see your saved location in the list. Click the Use button for the location you saved. The base station will enter the fixed mode and the status will show Using FixedLLA. In the future, if you set the base station in the same location, you do not need to conduct survey again, just click the Use button that corresponds to the location you have saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:168
#: e16a4ed4661e41ce918bc55d3058ed90
msgid "Rover Module and Autopilot Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:169
#: bd2a8990bd114f6880cee9c0602e5e2e
msgid "After the base station is set up, you can turn on the UAV. Using the same Mission Planner to connect the telemetry module, the base station data will be transmitted through telemetry module to the HERE + rover module on the UAV. In the Mission Planner main page, you can see the current GPS status displayed as RTK Float / RTK Fixed / 3D RTK, indicating that the positioning of the UAV has entered the RTK mode. RTK Float is a floating-point solution; RTK Fixed is a fixed solution. RTK Fixed mode has a higher accuracy and requires better signal strength. 3D RTK is unified saying of RTK Float / RTK in the Mission Planner Chinese version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:174
#: 51cfcba6ec0240d39ac33c3723c3afac
msgid "In the SurveyIn Acc input box, key in the absolute accuracy of base station you wish to achieve, in the unit of meters (for example, 0.50 means 50cm accuracy). In the Time(s) input box, key in a reference time in seconds. Depending on your desired accuracy, the base station may take more than your input time to achieve the desired accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:179
#: ee1d2cd99fab4159bd8a6e4514392060
msgid "Select the COM port for the base station and press Connect (the baud rate drop-down normally does not need to be set because it is automatically detected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:180
#: 46027e5db3ba49e5abeef9104772321b
msgid "\"M8P autoconfig\" should be checked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:185
#: 824d0b44ef63440995c7aa004513831a
msgid "The satellite information will be visualized as green bars as shown in the screen shot below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:190
#: 45e0a5479d6a4fd39dde84f0f8f7167d
msgid "A line of text will indicate the current status of the surveying: SurveyIn indicates whether the survey has achieved the desired accuracy of base station, it will show ‘true’ when the survey has been completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:193
#: bf1698f3611c4ab086621d351148f7d4
msgid "InProgress shows whether the survey is still ongoing. A completed survey of the current base position is indicated by the status messages SurveyIn Valid: True, and InProgress: false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:195
#: 1a1c5f5a43e44e41acfb4080067daf92
msgid "Duration: the duration of the survey in seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:197
#: 4c06f2f709a34a99815fdeb3a870d1e4
msgid "Obs: number of observations used for the survey"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:199
#: e25f61e3f9a6478199ca4d5617552675
msgid "Acc: current accuracy in meters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:201
#: 806844d48504440ca29c4dea2c688e56
msgid "When the survey is completed as indicated by the SurveyIn: True message, you may click the ‘Save current pos’ button and enter a name for the saved position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:202
#: 8e46417e6d9a4c829f574226fc04a190
msgid "The RTK messages from base station is sent to vehicle by MAVLink message. In the main HUD of Mission Planer, the GPS status should display RTK Fix or RTK Float"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:207
#: 276b32900343445595966dc10d543024
msgid "The information of the saved position will be displayed in the table as shown in the screen shot below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:212
#: 073a1dabf740400799ab018c4c9b04c2
msgid "The saved position can be used the next time you set up the base station in the exact same location. However, if you change to another location for surveying, please ensure you clear the position information in the dialogue box that pops up when you click ‘Enter Base Position’. Otherwise, the previously saved point will be taken every time you connect to the base module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:215
#: f49d91faf4294537bdf95a292cb0d33c
msgid "Use U-centre for live data recording/replaying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:216
#: 0a197839c88c4393bf27d614d6b3a8ad
msgid "One function of the U-center is to record the base / rover module data for later analysis. Firstly, when the base or rover module is already connected to U-center (in the same way it is connected when updating firmware), click the following bug icon to turn on the debug message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:221
#: caa7f60051b0442f9a120939b492e3ff
msgid "Then, click into View -> message view -> UBX -> RXM -> RTCM (RTCM input status), right click to enable message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:226
#: e1ac682cd3ba4afaacc3b7eaedf942f0
msgid "Finally, click on the red recording icon on the upper left corner of the interface (shown below), select an address to save the recording, click OK, the recording will begin. When recording is stopped, the recording will appear in the previously saved address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:231
#: e9fa267f193f4fcf980f9212da0d2039
msgid "To play the recorded data, click the green play icon, select a playback speed, select the specified address of your stored data file, then the data will be played."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:237
#: 4a1e3a3fb30344e9a84a869e06db2e95
msgid "Use U-Centre for debugging/advanced configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:238
#: 38f85ccc0c564d958e2aac6c9db4962a
msgid "-Check Status of Base Station. Connect the base module to U-center software, check the display box in the upper right corner of the interface, Fix Mode section is displayed as TIME. If Fix Mode does not enter TIME, the current state of the base station is not sufficient to allow the rover module to enter RTK mode. As shown in the figure below, Fix Mode is displayed in 3D mode, hence the RTK standard has not yet been reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:244
#: 5219b308118f44b9b1748049ad06b03d
msgid "The possible reasons for Base station not entering TIME Mode: Firstly, the signal received by base station is not strong enough. To check the satellite strength received by base station, see the bottom right corner of the software interface. The vertical bars in the box indicate satellites strength received by the current base station. A vertical bar represents a satellite (GPS or Beidou / GLONASS, depending on the choice of satellite systems). TIME Mode of base station requires: 5 GPS satellite signals +2 GLONASS satellite signals in the strength of 40 or more; or 5 GPS satellite signals +3 Beidou satellite signal in the strength of 40 or more. As shown in the figure below, only one satellite strength is higher than 40, the signal condition does not meet the RTK standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:249
#: e152e5fb7fd241208db6398e404a50da
msgid "Secondly, the user input of survey-in accuracy requirement is too strict to achieve, or the base station has not yet completed the surveying process. Using U-centre for survey-in setup, please refer to section c) in this chapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:251
#: f44434fdf669464cb20b4efb3b6c4518
msgid "-Check whether Rover receives base correction data(Timeout). After the base station enters the TIME Mode, it is necessary to transmit the RTCM data to the rover, for rover to enter RTK modes. Therefore, a real-time and efficient communication between rover and base station is necessary for good RTK positioning performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:254
#: 252f1ed8c5134433ab31af80e958f899
msgid "Check whether there is a delay in the data transmission between the mobile station and the base station, connect the rover module to U-center (or replay the data log to inspect a previous operation). Go to Messages view -> NMEA -> GxGGA directory to see Age of DGNSS Corr parameters. This parameter represents the time at which the rover did not receive the base station data. In the case of the default base station message frequency 1HZ, if this parameter exceeds 1s, there is a certain delay in the data transmission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:256
#: 1222a8f9254049e2b24150c332cbefd5
msgid "-Set Survey-in/Fixed mode for base station. Similar to Mission Planner RTK Inject page, U-center can also be used to set the base station survey-in time and accuracy. Enter the Messages view option, UBX's CGF menu, enter the TMODE3 tab. Select 1.Survey-in under the Mode drop-down option, and set the survey time (and the minimum time required for the base station to survey). The survey-in current status can be viewed in the NAV-> SVIN page in Message View."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:262
#: d07262ad2b5f45d9852ed3126408fae3
msgid "The base station can also be set to Fixed Mode. When the base station's current precise geographic coordinates are known, the coordinates can be entered directly into the base station, which saves the time required for surveying. In the TMODE3 page, select Fixed mode in the drop-down list, and then enter the precise known base station coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:264
#: 97b0e658b502431aa16b2fea1934364c
msgid "After setting the survey or fixed mode, click the Send button at the bottom left of the page to transfer the modified data to the base station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:266
#: 8b33424231134b88867f6c8d550d3494
msgid "-Use Beidou/GLonass. The uBlox 1.30 firmware uses the GPS + GLONASS navigation system for location services by default. If you want to change to GPS + Beidou navigation system, you need to enter the Messages view -> UBX -> CGF -> GNSS directory, cancel the tick on GLONASS Enable option, and then check the Beidou Enable option. After the selection, click send to complete the change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:272
#: 8d94e4b394134d0a89a865efe8853d7b
msgid "To save the current settings, go to the Messages view -> UBX -> CFG (Configuration) page and click the Save current configuration option, then click Send (as shown below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:279
#: a48af5fef8ae44a08cf311b3b27f1e5f
msgid "Base station and rover should use the same navigation system configuration, or rover will not be able to enter RTK modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:281
#: 9b2ff320e6ee41b88df610db389e11ad
msgid "-Base module I/O port and protocol setup. UBlox M8P chip supports a variety of input and output protocols, including USB, UART, I2C and so on. The HERE + base station module uses the USB port for data communication and RTK outputs. If you need to confirm the current settings, go to the Messages view -> UBX -> CFG -> PRT directory and select 3-USB in the Target field. The correct input and output protocols are shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:288
#: f439b20ed50d4e7584ed003d9d61824f
msgid "If you want to use more output protocols (such as UART), you can also select the output protocol and a specific message combination on this page. If you want to set a string of specific messages to output under a variety of protocols, you can go to the Messages view -> UBX -> CGF -> MSG directory, select a specific message, and then check the type of protocol you want to output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:290
#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:298
#: 1c0863bd67374f2c96211dc7ab33894e
#: f6961e2ea41e4ce6a454a9b7914040c5
msgid "To save the current settings, go to the Messages view -> UBX -> CFG (Configuration) page and click the Save current configuration option, then click Send."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-here-plus-gps.rst:292
#: e015b114ec964e7ea1455e3febdacc0d
msgid "-Change Rover module output rate. By default, the output frequency of the position information by the rover module is 1HZ. If you need to speed up the position output frequency, you can enter the Messages view -> UBX -> CGF -> RATE directory, change the Measurement Period. For example, the measurement period is changed to 200 ms and the measurement frequency will be increased to 5 Hz."
msgstr ""

